From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: L1521 uniform keep gaps closed (EDEN_UP_L1521_KEEP_GAPS), off by default

Port of zortos293/Lichii PR #1521, commit 45d0fb6 (Zortos, with Lucas Borges; "close uniform keep
gaps and copy only the fast-draw delta's ranges in use", from #1161). Ported by reading onto our
EDEN_UP_L949_UBO_KEEP (Lichii #949 keeps, delta draws only; upstream's are #1441's).

With EDEN_UP_L1521_KEEP_GAPS=1 (exact "1", read once; needs EDEN_UP_L949_UBO_KEEP=1, which needs
EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW=1):
- Each submitted guest command list ends uniform keeps: on the split, a FastDrawNeutral deferred
  call bumps Nx2FastDraw::g_keep_submits in order on the back (draw reuse itself goes on); without
  the split it is bumped where the list is pushed. BeginGraphicsUniforms keeps nothing when the
  count moved since the previous draw. Guest CPU writes before a submit go unseen on pages the
  caches don't watch.
- DMA copies from memory no GPU wrote, DMA clears and in-place inline uploads (InlineMemory) are
  noted to the keeps (NoteUniformWrite); before, only a DMA copy with GPU data was.
- The keep verifier (EDEN_UP_L949_UBO_KEEP_VERIFY) compares only ranges RebindKeptUniform would
  bind again (KeptUniformMatches: same range, same command buffer).

Not taken, and why: TakeDelta (copy only the ranges in use): our TakeReusableDraw already reads
g_delta in place and copies only the device ranges for the keeps. The GPU memory compare
(keep.gpu_memory): our keeps are only on delta draws, which TakeReusableDraw allows only with the
same MemoryManager. The puller acquire notes: every acquire path of ours already ends draw reuse
(Break(Fence), or EndFastDrawAtAcquire's deferred call), so no delta draw, and no keep, crosses
one. The overflow -> no_uniform_keeps rename: done by 0559. Tests: not built here.

Line (HW_GPU, the first 16 events, then powers of two): "EDEN_UP_L1521_KEEP_GAPS: keeps ended by
a submitted list N, noted writes: DMA copies from memory no GPU wrote N, DMA clears N, inline
uploads in place N; verify skipped N (kept so far N)".

Effect: fewer uniform keeps (safer), never more. Off: one bool per submit list, DMA copy/clear,
inline upload and keep-verify bind. Memory: none to speak of. Not in the kept-store stamp:
buffer_cache*.h, uniform_stream_reuse.h, gpu_thread.cpp, nx2_fast_draw.h (KEEPS THE STORE).
---
